    "q-136881": {
      "dom_id": "step-q136881",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A discrete random variable $X$ has the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. Find $\\text{E}[{e}^{X}].$\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "For a discrete random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}r(x)f(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{e}^{X}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{e}^{x}\\,f(x) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+{e}^{0}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+{e}^{1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+1\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+e\\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{8}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{e}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}+6+e}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
