    "q-136882": {
      "dom_id": "step-q136882",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A discrete random variable $X$ has the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below.  Find $\\text{E}[(2X+1)^{2}].$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |",
      "worked_solution": "For a discrete random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}r(x)f(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)=(2x+1)^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[(2X+1)^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(2x+1)^{2}\\,f(x) \\\\  & =(2+1)^{2}\\cdot 0.2+(4+1)^{2}\\cdot 0.3+(6+1)^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =9\\cdot 0.2+25\\cdot 0.3+49\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.8+7.5+24.5 \\\\  & =33.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
